From 7a96edfa1fc07e981631352e3becc14cc9eb4e45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 11:48:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(monitor): surface-only PR auto-monitor workflow
 (35ee8d78)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add .github/workflows/pr-monitor.yml — a GitHub Actions workflow that fires on
PR events (opened/synchronize/reopened, review submitted, review comment,
issue_comment, check_suite completed) and keeps ONE sticky PR comment current
with the PR's unresolved review threads (grouped BY AUTHOR, any author) and
failing/pending checks, so async review-bot/human feedback never rots.

Author-agnostic by construction: threads come from Forge's own agnostic gather
(forge shepherd <pr> --bundle --json -> lib/pr-bundle.js -> GraphQL
reviewThreads{isResolved} across all authors), never a name-list. The monitor
SURFACES state only — it never merges and never posts a pass/fail verdict
(auto-verdict awaits the trustworthy-shepherd redesign f1af41ef, out of scope).

New pure renderer lib/pr-monitor/render-sticky.js (TDD, 6 tests) turns one
read-only bundle into the sticky Markdown; the workflow upserts it by hidden
HTML marker. Optional NEUTRAL check run is informational by construction.

Refs: 35ee8d78 (no-auto-trigger fix), b5c154cd (safe surface part), c2d398e5
(constant-monitor epic).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
